# arithmetic: add, subtract, multiply, divide, and when...otherwise
create a variable called total as an integer with a value of 100
create a variable called one as an integer with a value of 1
create a variable called ten as an integer with a value of 10
create a variable called result as an integer with a value of 0

add the variable one to the variable total
write out the variable total
subtract the variable ten from the variable total
write out the variable total
multiply the variable ten by the variable total
write out the variable total
divide the variable ten by the variable total
write out the variable total

when the variable total is equal to 91 write out the string "odd but correct"
when the variable total is equal to 999 write out the string "wrong" otherwise write out the string "otherwise fires"
when the variable total is greater than 90 write out the string "still big" otherwise write out the string "not big"